EN:
Using the ISRU as an example you can think of the core as the 
furnace that melts down Ore to produces resources. This process 
has three important thermal points:
 • The core has an optimum temperature, with inadequate cooling it will overheat (and be 
     less efficient);
 • The process discards a lot of the thermal energy through exhaust directly to the environment 
     (for drills you can think of this as the tailings of the drilling process);
 • Some of the heat does "soak" into the internal component of the part;
